# Citation metadata for jev-compactor (https://citation-file-format.github.io).
# GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" widget from this file. Update `version` and
# `date-released` when tagging a release; add a `doi` under `identifiers` if a Zenodo DOI is minted.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use jev-compactor in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "jev-compactor"
abstract: >-
  Deterministic context compaction and safety gating for AI agents, powered by TypeSafe's Jev.
  A TypeScript library, CLI and MCP server that keeps an agent's messages verbatim, drops the
  ones Jev judges irrelevant to the goal, and flags or blocks destructive actions in the same
  pass. Works with OpenAI, Anthropic, LangChain and plain message arrays.
authors:
